course: dictionary
lesson: 13336
title: One word, many places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gymnasium is a large room or building with equipment for sport and exercise. Use the clues around the word: «The gymnasium is full of mats, ropes and balls.» Mats, ropes and balls are sports equipment, so a gymnasium must be a sports hall.
explain: «Our class walks to the gymnasium for PE on Tuesdays.» PE means lessons where you move, play and do sport. The clue tells you the gymnasium is the place where those lessons happen.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another country or in history. «In ancient Greece, young men trained at the gymnasium.» Here it was a place for training and studying, not just a room of equipment. Always check the clues in each sentence.
fact: A gymnasium is a large room or building with equipment for sport and exercise.
fact: Gymnasium can be shortened to gym, as in «Let's go to the gym».
fact: The plural of gymnasium is gymnasiums or gymnasia.
fact: In Germany, the Netherlands and Ukraine, a gymnasium is a kind of secondary school.
fact: In ancient Greece, a gymnasium was a place where young men trained and studied.
exercise: «The gymnasium is full of mats, ropes and balls.» What is a gymnasium? | A small shop that sells sweets | *A large room with equipment for sport and exercise | A type of cloud that brings rain | A kind of bread baked in a tin
exercise: What is the short form of gymnasium? | gum | game | gymnast | *gym
exercise: «My cousin in Germany goes to a Gymnasium.» What kind of place is that? | A church | A swimming pool | *A kind of secondary school | A shop for sports clothes
test: «The school assembly was held in the gymnasium.» Where was the assembly? | Outside in the rain | In the car park | *In the gymnasium | In the library
test: «In ancient Greece, young men trained at the gymnasium.» What was a gymnasium in ancient Greece? | *A place where young men trained and studied | A market for buying food | A kind of ship | A temple to the gods
exam: «Let's go to the gym after lunch.» Gym here means what? | A type of drink | A quiet place to read | A kind of school bag | *A room for sport and exercise
